The Cargo and CMake production targets now compile author_a FSM, manager,
container, original map core and time-domain controller, plus the author-A
bspline/A*/polynomial files under upstream/. Old native/src and legacy include
implementations are retained for provenance, not compiled into this target.

Explicit user exceptions: do not freeze translation at a fixed 0.8 rad heading
error; do not replace the final business goal with an earlier free point.

Necessary host adaptations: ROS transport/time/parameter/visualization removal;
persistent per-navigation-session state; real platform limits and calibrated
body reference; original-author step-aware collision-band parameter mapping;
independent pre-existing business boundary/forbidden constraints; real registered
world frames and separately labelled static occupancy fixtures; cancellation,
source validity and physical stop evidence remain outside the author algorithm.
Original A calculation timeouts use steady wall time, trajectory time uses one
injected host clock. Console diagnostics go to stderr, preserving the host JSON
protocol. Full physical standing dimensions and simulation judge are unchanged.

Additional documented stairs corrections (2026-10-21): retain the original
ceil/XY inflation broadphase and original occupied-cell probability source,
but resolve vertical candidates against positive-volume intersection with the
calibrated collision band. This removes query-cell phase enlargement without
shrinking the candidate stencil. Explicit static occupied-volume fixtures do
not inject their already-represented exposed top boundary as another voxel;
real measured ground and registered LiDAR returns remain unchanged.

Local height initialization and A* search guidance retain the complete ordered
PCT route before author waypoint decimation, with global-reference time/route-
arc association and collision-segment-local parameter binding. This replaces
straight start-to-end height interpolation, not the author optimizer objective,
Z-gradient freeze, search budget, or controller. Boundary LS fitting and search
endpoint residuals remain; guidance is not a proof of exact terrain adherence.
The original unknown-space policy is unchanged. All real physical dimensions,
independent motion validation, target and acceptance tolerances are unchanged.

The historical integrated-B notice below is retained because its retired source
and attribution are still present. It is not the current SCAN algorithm source.

